<title>USA: Bell Atlantic, NYNEX prepare defence.</title>
<headline>Bell Atlantic, NYNEX prepare defence.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bell Atlantic Corp and NYNEX Corp are stepping up preparations for a legal counter-attack they can use if the Justice Department moves to block their proposed $23 billion merger, the Wall Street Journal said in Thursday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>One executive was quoted in the newspaper as saying people inside the companies' executive offices were &quot;in the dumps,&quot; expecting the deal to be rejected, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Some observers think there is a more than 50 percent chance antitrust regulators would sue to block the deal, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
